Greetings, I tried to make a system where it will show a picture based on the current mapID and also don't show the picture if the there's no picture file based on a said mapID exist. Here's the code.
JavaScript:
var MapDisplay = MapDisplay || {};

MapDisplay.showMap = function() {

    // Retrieve the current map's ID.
    const mapId = $gameMap.mapId();
    // Retrieve map images path
    const imgPath = "Maps/";
    //Combine the path and name file
    const fullPath = imgPath + mapId;
    const MapID_pngformat = mapId+".png";




    // Set up the parameters for displaying the picture
    const pictureId = 10;       
    const origin = 1;         
    const x = 512;             
    const y = 256;             
    const scaleX = 100;       
    const scaleY = 100;       
    const opacity = 255;       
    const blendMode = 0;       




pictureExists = function(MapID_pngformat) {
    const fs = require ("fs");
    return fs.existsSync("./img/pictures/Maps" + MapID_pngformat);
};




    if(pictureExists){
        //If the image file exist then show it.
    $gameScreen.showPicture(pictureId, fullPath, origin, x, y, scaleX, scaleY, opacity, blendMode);
    }else{
        //Otherwise call a common event
        $gameTemp.reserveCommonEvent(159);
    }



};
My biggest struggle is with how to actually detect the said image files. I've been scouring through the forum and so far, there's no good and consistent solution for RPG Maker MZ.
Thanks in advance!

Your
pictureExists
function looks fine, although you should really add a
const, let or var
keyword when declaring it. However in your conditional statement you're not calling the function, it should have closing parenthesis after the name, like so.
JavaScript:
if(pictureExists(/*mapId*/)){
     //If the image file exist then show it.
}}
another thing to take not on is that this will only work for desktop builds of your game, this will not work for browser deployments.

