JavaScript:
function UrlExists(url) {
  var http = new XMLHttpRequest();
  try{
    http.open('HEAD', url, false);
    http.send();
    return http.status!=404;
  }catch(ex){return false;}
}
This is the code I'm using. It just works but sync option for XMLHttpRequest may freeze the game if the server is slow in response.
Another method is building a complete file list after you deploy the game, and check if the file exists.

